{"nodes": [{"id": "brain_knowledge_07_figure_programme_figure_programme", "label": "Figure Programme \u2014 Specification for the Dissertation's Floats", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/07_figure_programme.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_07_figure_programme_float_slot_arithmetic", "label": "Float-Slot Arithmetic and the 60-Word Caption Reserve", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/07_figure_programme.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reading 420 words of headroom as one oversized caption would breach the caption cap and spend the whole headroom on one float; it is seven slots at 60 words. Nineteen floats are specified so the twentieth slot absorbs overruns without a late negotiation."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_07_figure_programme_f1_fig_blocks", "label": "F1 fig:blocks \u2014 The Four-Block Split", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/07_figure_programme.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A flowchart shows dependency but not ordering, and the defect being fixed is temporal, so a horizontal timeline is used instead. Net -165 words, the largest single saving in the programme."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_07_figure_programme_f2_fig_origins", "label": "F2 fig:origins \u2014 Rolling-Origin Protocol (demoted to Appendix C)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/07_figure_programme.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cheapest of the seven to lose: its net word cost was roughly zero, so demoting it saves no prose either way while shedding the caption cost."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_07_figure_programme_f3_fig_pipeline", "label": "F3 fig:pipeline \u2014 The Method Pipeline", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/07_figure_programme.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two separate figures were rejected on cost: they share most of their boxes, so the deployment architecture goes to an appendix at zero cost and the body carries the method only."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_07_figure_programme_f4_fig_drift", "label": "F4 fig:drift \u2014 Residual-Scale Drift and the Exchangeability Violation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/07_figure_programme.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A bar chart of four time-quartile means cannot separate a drift in level from a change in composition, and composition is the finding."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_07_figure_programme_f5_fig_validity_efficiency", "label": "F5 fig:validity-efficiency \u2014 Coverage Against Interval Width", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/07_figure_programme.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A bar chart of Winkler scores adds ink without a reading; the scatter shows the two components the score compounds, which the score conceals."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_07_figure_programme_f6_fig_sensitivity", "label": "F6 fig:sensitivity \u2014 Catch Rate Against Deviation Magnitude", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/07_figure_programme.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The cost sweep was rejected as a chart because it is degenerate: misses and false alarms are constant across all ratios, so the sweep would plot a linear reweighting of two constants. The degeneracy stays a reported sentence."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_07_figure_programme_f7_fig_nulls", "label": "F7 fig:nulls \u2014 Paired Differences for the Weather and Pooling Arms", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/07_figure_programme.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bars of near-identical means invite ranking by eye, which is the exact error the null asserts cannot be made."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_07_figure_programme_a_f1_screening_flow", "label": "A-F1 Corpus Screening Flow (no diagram drawn)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/07_figure_programme.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_07_figure_programme_appendix_floats", "label": "Appendix Floats A-F1 to A-F7", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/07_figure_programme.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_07_figure_programme_float_blockers_b0_b7", "label": "Float Blockers B0-B7", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/07_figure_programme.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Resolved before a figure is built rather than after; the table itself went stale once the blockers were worked without anyone returning to it, which is the failure mode of a state store nobody points at."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_07_figure_programme_run_list_r0_r4", "label": "Run List R0-R4 Under the Rerun Gate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/07_figure_programme.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_07_figure_programme_events_fourth_location", "label": "The `events` Fourth Square Location", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/07_figure_programme.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_07_figure_programme_boundary_not_exclusion", "label": "Ruled: Boundary, Not Exclusion", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/07_figure_programme.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The unit of analysis is a trading venue with an opening calendar against which a rhythm can be learned; `events` has no site and no calendar however many rows it carries. The volume figure was demoted to corroboration because a volume justification has the shape of a data-driven exclusion threshold, which is exactly what triggers R83."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_07_figure_programme_corpus_silence", "label": "Where the Corpus Is Silent", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/07_figure_programme.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A convention traceable to a cited work is stated as such and a convention that is not is declared; A-F1 is justified from reporting standards rather than from corpus precedent, and the caption must not imply otherwise."}, {"id": "brain_knowledge_07_figure_programme_dangling_reference_finding", "label": "Five Dangling \\ref Sites With No Matching \\label", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/knowledge/07_figure_programme.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "brain_knowledge_07_figure_programme_figure_programme", "target": "brain_knowledge_07_figure_programme_float_slot_arithmetic", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "brain/knowledge/07_figure_programme.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "brain_knowledge_07_figure_programme_figure_programme",